  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.71:\n\t\t- Fixed: GetResourceGroupByFullPathAsync returned null for any group whose path contains a\n\t\t  segment with leading or trailing whitespace, even though the group exists - callers saw\n\t\t  \"no such path\" for a group plainly present in the portal. LogicMonitor's filter endpoint\n\t\t  silently trims whitespace in filter values, so the Eq on fullPath matched nothing. Verified\n\t\t  against a live portal: the filter returns 0 results for such a path and 1 for an otherwise\n\t\t  identical control, while the tree node free search returns the group with its whitespace\n\t\t  intact. The fallback already used for parentheses was therefore capable of resolving these\n\t\t  groups all along; it was simply never reached, because the trigger only tested for\n\t\t  parentheses. That trigger now also covers whitespace, tested segment by segment rather than\n\t\t  on the whole path, since an interior segment can carry a space without the full path looking\n\t\t  untrimmed. Ordinary paths continue to use the cheaper filter.\n\t\t- Note: GetDashboardGroupByFullPathAsync and GetWebsiteGroupByFullPathAsync have neither this\n\t\t  workaround nor the parentheses one, and are likely affected in principle. Unchanged for now,\n\t\t  as neither has been observed failing.",
